<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>CsrCarrierProbe</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>CsrCarrierProbe</RootNamespace>
    <Description>Diagnostic for Certus security issue #548 (CRA risks R02, R03) and Certus-Security #15. Submits PKCS#10 requests that carry subject alternative name content, and requested Application Policies, to a live ADCS CA through several attribute carriers the product's finalize parser does not read: the Microsoft certificate extensions attribute (szOID_CERT_EXTENSIONS 1.3.6.1.4.1.311.2.1.14), the enrolment name and value pair attribute (1.3.6.1.4.1.311.13.2.1), and a second value of the standard PKCS#9 extensionRequest. Reports what the CA puts in the issued certificate. Answers, before any server hardening is trusted, whether ADCS honours any of these carriers on an enrollee supplies subject template.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- A source link, not a ProjectReference, following tools/DeviceAttestProbe:
         the probe keeps the tools/ convention of standing alone with no assembly
         dependency on the product, and Certus.Core would drag EF Core,
         BouncyCastle, MailKit and Serilog behind it for a self contained publish
         that only needs one static class. The template guard and its character
         scanner are a security invariant (issue #175, CVE-2026-54121): the probe
         builds the CertificateTemplate attribute through the product's own guard
         rather than interpolating it, so this is never the one place in the repo
         that hands a live CA an unchecked request attribute string. A copy would
         be free to drift. Any dependency the guard grows needs the same line, and
         only `dotnet build tools/CsrCarrierProbe` catches a missed link, since
         the probe is outside Certus.sln and the test suite. -->
    <Compile Include="../../src/Certus.Core/Security/DeceptiveCharacters.cs"
             Link="DeceptiveCharacters.cs" />
    <Compile Include="../../src/Certus.Core/Adcs/AdcsRequestAttributes.cs"
             Link="AdcsRequestAttributes.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
